<title>CHINA: China corn imports down sharply in Jan-Aug.</title>
<headline>China corn imports down sharply in Jan-Aug.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's corn imports fell to 440,000 tonnes in the first eight months of 1996, down 81.6 percent compared with year-ago period, customs figures showed on Monday.</p>
<p>China imported almost no corn in August, the figures showed.</p>
<p>China exported 120,000 tonnes of corn in the first eight months, up by 13.6 percent compared with the same year-ago period, it said. Exports in August alone were 70,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>China imported 5.18 million tonnes of corn in 1995. Exports for the year fell to 110,000 tonnes after China officially banned corn exports late in 1994 to try to curb rising prices.</p>
</text>
